---
title: "Krewire Contributors — Home of the Open Source Collective"
description: "The home for engineers, architects, and AI agent guilds crafting an autonomous, sustainable Go digital ecosystem at near-zero cost."
layout: Landing
---

<div class="contributors-portal">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="eyebrow" data-i18n="hero.eyebrow">◈ OPEN SOURCE COLLECTIVE · AUTONOMOUS GO ECOSYSTEM</div>
        <h1 data-i18n-html="hero.title_html">Build the Future of Go.<br>Together, Autonomously.</h1>
        <p class="lead" data-i18n="hero.lead">The home for contributors, architects, and AI agent guilds engineering an autonomous, sustainable digital ecosystem in Go. From unified workloads and zero-cost IaC to AI agent orchestration — engineered in Indonesia for engineers worldwide.</p>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a class="btn primary" href="#get-started" data-i18n="hero.cta_start">Start Contributing →</a>
          <a class="btn" href="#repositories" data-i18n="hero.cta_repos">Explore Repositories</a>
        </div>
        <div class="meta" data-i18n="hero.meta">Go 1.22+ · Spec-Driven Development (KWF) · Strict Quality Gates · Human & AI Synergy</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-art">
        {{component "CodeWindow" .}}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TRUST BAR -->
  <section class="trust">
    <div class="trust-inner">
      <span class="trust-label" data-i18n="trust.label">Collective Ecosystem</span>
      <div class="trust-items">
        <span data-i18n-html="trust.repos_html"><b>6</b> Active Repositories</span>
        <span class="dot">·</span>
        <span data-i18n-html="trust.workloads_html"><b>8</b> Unified Workloads</span>
        <span class="dot">·</span>
        <span data-i18n-html="trust.native_html"><b>100%</b> Native Go</span>
        <span class="dot">·</span>
        <span data-i18n-html="trust.gates_html"><b>3</b> Strict Quality Gates</span>
        <span class="dot">·</span>
        <span data-i18n="trust.cost">Near-Zero Cloud Cost</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PILLARS / PHILOSOPHY -->
  <section class="pillars" id="philosophy">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="pillars.badge">Philosophy</div>
        <h2 data-i18n="pillars.title">Engineered for Autonomy, Built for Longevity</h2>
        <p data-i18n="pillars.subtitle">Krewire is not just another web framework. It is an open architectural collective solving software fragmentation, ballooning cloud costs, and developer fatigue.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar-grid">
        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-icon">⚡</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="pillars.p1_title">Autonomous by Design</h3>
          <p data-i18n="pillars.p1_desc">Built from ground up to support self-healing, self-building pipelines, and native orchestration by autonomous AI agents (Guild).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-icon">📐</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="pillars.p2_title">Spec-Driven Development (SDD)</h3>
          <p data-i18n="pillars.p2_desc">Zero hand-waving. Every architectural boundary begins with formal specifications (<code>KWF-*</code>) and clear contract interfaces before implementation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-icon">🌱</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="pillars.p3_title">Near-Zero Cloud Cost</h3>
          <p data-i18n="pillars.p3_desc">Radical resource efficiency. Go standard-library minimalism designed to operate smoothly on $5 VPS nodes up to hyperscale infrastructure.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-icon">🤝</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="pillars.p4_title">Human-AI Synergy</h3>
          <p data-i18n="pillars.p4_desc">Specialized AI agent guilds act as first-class team members — auditing security, catching regressions, and helping contributors iterate faster.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CONTRIBUTOR BENEFITS & LIFETIME ACCESS -->
  <section class="benefits" id="benefits">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="benefits.badge">Contributor Privilege</div>
        <h2 data-i18n="benefits.title">Lifetime Access to Krewire's Paid Ecosystem</h2>
        <p data-i18n="benefits.subtitle">Genuine appreciation for true builders. By joining and actively contributing to the Krewire open source collective, you earn lifetime access to our upcoming commercial sub-products and premium ecosystem tools.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="benefit-grid">
        <div class="benefit-card highlight">
          <div class="benefit-badge" data-i18n="benefits.b1_badge">Core Privilege</div>
          <div class="benefit-icon">★</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="benefits.b1_title">Commercial Sub-Products Lifetime Access</h3>
          <p data-i18n="benefits.b1_desc">Receive free lifetime licenses for upcoming commercial Krewire products — including managed cloud orchestration tools, enterprise modules, and premium services.</p>
          <ul class="benefit-list">
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b1_i1">Free lifetime access to all paid Krewire commercial sub-products</li>
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b1_i2">Priority early-access releases and exclusive roadmap previews</li>
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b1_i3">Direct private collaboration channels with core maintainers</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-card condition">
          <div class="benefit-badge req" data-i18n="benefits.b2_badge">Strict Requirement</div>
          <div class="benefit-icon">⚡</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="benefits.b2_title">Active Contributions Required</h3>
          <p data-i18n="benefits.b2_desc">This privilege is a two-way commitment. Your access remains active as long as you regularly contribute and help nurture the ecosystem's growth.</p>
          <ul class="benefit-list">
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b2_i1">Submit PRs for new features, bugfixes, or kernel optimizations</li>
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b2_i2">Review open PRs and stress-test high-concurrency scenarios</li>
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b2_i3">Author KWF architecture specifications or comprehensive docs</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-card notice">
          <div class="benefit-badge warn" data-i18n="benefits.b3_badge">Revocation Policy</div>
          <div class="benefit-icon">⚠</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="benefits.b3_title">Revocable if Inactive or Dormant</h3>
          <p data-i18n="benefits.b3_desc">To protect community fairness and true meritocracy, commercial access licenses may be revoked at any time if a contributor becomes inactive or dormant over an extended period.</p>
          <ul class="benefit-list">
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b3_i1">Contributor activity and commits are periodically audited</li>
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b3_i2">Prolonged inactivity or dormancy leads to license deactivation</li>
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b3_i3">Access privileges can be promptly reinstated upon resumed contribution</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="benefit-policy-banner">
        <div class="policy-marker">◈</div>
        <div class="policy-text">
          <strong data-i18n="benefits.policy_title">Krewire Meritocracy Policy:</strong>
          <span data-i18n="benefits.policy_text">We believe those who lay the foundation should share in its fruits. Commercial access is free for all active contributors, provided ongoing dedication to the collective is consistently maintained.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- UNIFIED CODEBASE MATRIX & CONTRIBUTOR NAVIGATOR -->
  <section class="repos-nav" id="repositories">
    <span id="where-to-start" class="section-anchor"></span>
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="navigator.badge">Codebase Matrix &amp; Navigator</div>
        <h2 data-i18n="navigator.title">Core Repositories &amp; Where to Start</h2>
        <p data-i18n="navigator.subtitle">Match your skills and background to the right codebase, bootstrap your local environment in 30 seconds, and dive straight into active issues.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- FAST-TRACK ONE-LINE SETUP BANNER -->
      <div class="fast-setup-box">
        <div class="fast-setup-header">
          <div class="fast-setup-title">
            <span class="fast-icon">⚡</span>
            <strong data-i18n="navigator.one_line_title">One-Command Contributor Bootstrap</strong>
          </div>
          <span class="fast-setup-badge" data-i18n="navigator.one_line_badge">Recommended</span>
        </div>
        <p class="fast-setup-desc" data-i18n-html="navigator.one_line_desc_html">Automatically clones all ecosystem repositories, creates your <code>go.work</code> workspace, builds the <code>kiw</code> devtool, and validates compatibility contracts:</p>
        <div class="terminal-cmd-bar">
          <code id="setup-cmd">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/krewire/internal/main/scripts/setup.sh | bash</code>
          <button class="btn-copy" data-copy-cmd aria-label="Copy setup command">
            <span class="copy-text" data-i18n="navigator.copy_btn">Copy</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="fast-setup-meta">
          <span data-i18n="navigator.meta_prereq">Prerequisites: Go 1.22+ and Git</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span data-i18n="navigator.meta_zero">Zero manual configuration required</span>
        </div>
      </div>

